        "title": "New Lady Gaga performance streaming this Thursday exclusively on Apple Music",
        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/05/12/new-lady-gaga-concert-film-streaming-this-thursday-exclusively-on-apple-music/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/05/apple-music-lady-gag.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1358\" /></div><p>Apple today announced that <a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/getapplemusic\">Apple Music subscribers</a> will be able to stream a brand new Lady Gaga filmed live performance this Thursday, in which the artist performed tracks from her MAYHEM album.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>In fact, at 8 AM Pacific Time on May 14, anyone can tune in for free (no subscription required) to watch the live stream premiere. After the fact, it will be available to watch on demand for Apple Music subscribers.  </p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1051889\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/05/12/new-lady-gaga-concert-film-streaming-this-thursday-exclusively-on-apple-music/#more-1051889\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
        "type": "Technology",
